"""
Catalogue of minimum aberration two-level fractional factorial designs.

``_MA_GENERATORS[(n_factors, n_runs)] = (resolution, generators)``: the first
``log2(n_runs)`` factors are the base factors, and generator ``i`` defines
factor ``log2(n_runs) + i`` as the product of the listed base factors
(0-based).

The designs are published results:

* Chen, Sun & Wu (1993), "A catalogue of two-level and three-level fractional
  factorial designs with small runs", International Statistical Review 61(1),
  pp. 131-145 (up to 64 runs).
* Xu (2009), "Algorithmic construction of efficient fractional factorial
  designs with large run sizes", Technometrics 51(3), pp. 262-277, and
  Block & Mee (2005), "Resolution IV designs with 128 runs", Journal of
  Quality Technology 37(4), pp. 282-293, doi:10.1080/00224065.2005.11980331
  (128 runs).

The selection of the minimum aberration design per size (the first entry per
size) was taken from the design catalogue of the R package FrF2 by Ulrike
Groemping: Groemping (2014), "R package FrF2 for creating and analyzing
fractional factorial 2-level designs", Journal of Statistical Software 56(1),
pp. 1-56, doi:10.18637/jss.v056.i01.
"""

